#---
# purpose: "an argument outside every member of a cross-kind union @spec domain is rejected at compile time"
# expect: diagnostic
# diagnostic.code: spec/violation
#---
#
# # spec_violation_cross_kind_union
#
# `M.f`'s domain is the cross-kind union `:first | {:acc, a}`. The atom
# `:third` is accepted by neither member, so the call is a fatal
# `spec/violation` on every path. The union's atom member must not shield
# an uncovered witness from the veto (it only accepts witnesses that
# actually land in it, like `:first`).
defmodule M do
  @spec f(:first | {:acc, a}) :: a
  fn f(:first), do: panic("empty")
  fn f({:acc, acc}), do: acc
end

fn main(), do: dbg(M.f(:third))
